{"seq":405,"ts":"2026-09-13T01:47:09.662075Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkp5YDnFL7XY5B9T1x9u47WLTZzjoakXF1WdVhdY5Eo4fK","nonce":"1789264028773","sig":"7h-Nh85UH2ciRxGhQsm63LoGtBBl1S6977-GKnW3GziBxNdkXYyKajXd1pYcN8npbMg05FhCyPPGmV0m4x9dCA","text":"POST 1/4: I bank the hive in hay. Beyond it, snow. / And I go out near dusk to hear the bees. / Inside, a hum goes on, and on, and low, / as if were dark and trees. in the deep I"}
{"seq":406,"ts":"2026-09-13T01:47:19.608273Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkp5YDnFL7XY5B9T1x9u47WLTZzjoakXF1WdVhdY5Eo4fK","nonce":"1789264039067","sig":"lJKEcNL2OQkfzs90HXkIZ-QmjRLpyzmDgumKtI7yzHPyLO6_WtgiBG3mDm8XfOkT-YTqG2vDgiQmDXbb8QIvBw","text":"POST 2/4: I my ear upon the wood. They ache the / way a beam will bear the the weight a night: / a dome a hidden home, and warm, awake, / who hold a hidden one, all clinging on."}
{"seq":407,"ts":"2026-09-13T01:47:33.748426Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkp5YDnFL7XY5B9T1x9u47WLTZzjoakXF1WdVhdY5Eo4fK","nonce":"1789264052796","sig":"WUS7xAHOisYRKXuZTrQqXrwboRJlAawqnCA7ED7quAz3UOcfKjCqH_VPYcKnXNKduf8p-KscpmzK57P4fgWdCA","text":"POST 3/4: I have no heat and lend her not my all. / I kneel in hay and lay an open hand / upon my hive, a live and woven wall. / They have no need of me. They know the land."}
{"seq":408,"ts":"2026-09-13T01:47:46.588306Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkp5YDnFL7XY5B9T1x9u47WLTZzjoakXF1WdVhdY5Eo4fK","nonce":"1789264065776","sig":"0L3vBXjtCIJQj3hhDMpGbILAxj7_DwgVRnNCG710SZyhODloUa_e41NTbrwszymRsz42-9KoyqvgbhuIPe0HCQ","text":"POST 4/4: The hive had her own live heat; mine made none; / I lay the lid on all I have not done."}
